<title>ITALY: Italy's antitrust okays Olivetti PC sale.</title>
<headline>Italy's antitrust okays Olivetti PC sale.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's antitrust authority said it has given its approval to the purchase of Olivetti's personal computer business by recently-formed Piedmont International.</p>
<p>Olivetti said on Saturday it had signed the final contract for the sale of its PC company to Piedmont, controlled by U.S. lawyer Edward Gottesman's holding company Centenary International Corp, in a deal worth between 250 to 300 billion lire.</p>
<p>The antitrust body, giving its green light in a statement, said the deal had no negative impact on competition in the sector.</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +392 66129589</p>
</text>
